Verdict: MAJOR

Findings:
- [severity: critical] OCIMF coefficient source remains an open engineering input — The plan allows implementation to either “locate” a CSV or create a “bounded digitized fixture,” but does not define the approved source, vessel class/curve basis, digitization method, licensing/provenance constraints, interpolation rules, or validation tolerances. This can change B1528 SIROCCO force results materially. Recommended plan change: add a pre-implementation gate requiring the exact OCIMF generic coefficient source to be selected, cited, legally safe, versioned, and independently validated before any force implementation proceeds.

- [severity: critical] Plan invents calculation physics in pseudocode — The formulas `q * frontal_current_area * CXc`, `q * lateral_current_area * CYc`, `q * lateral_current_area * L_ref * CMc`, and `derived_or_reported_lever_arm` are not tied to a cited OCIMF convention or the existing `ocimf.py` API. That risks mixing coefficient definitions, reference areas, moment reference lengths, and sign conventions. Recommended plan change: replace pseudocode formulas with “use existing OCIMF calculation API or a cited formula contract,” and list the exact reference areas, reference length, datum, coefficient sign convention, and unit conversions to be tested.

- [severity: high] Rudder default model is still under-specified — The plan says “simple area/drag-style calculation as default” but leaves coefficient/reference basis open. That is an unapproved physics decision, especially since the alternate existing/Barrass-family model will be shown side-by-side. Recommended plan change: define the simple rudder model equation, coefficient source, lever arm, sign convention, and expected default-case value before approval, or make approval explicitly conditional on a follow-up user decision.

- [severity: high] TDD lacks independent numerical oracles — Tests such as `test_issue_2760_current_default_sample_calculation` and rudder side-by-side checks say “deterministic X/Y/N within tolerance” but do not name expected coefficients, expected signs, expected values, tolerances, or independent hand-calculation fixtures. This would let implementation bless its own math. Recommended plan change: add table-driven golden cases for at least heading `0`, `+5`, `-5` and rudder `0`, `+28`, including coefficient values, kN/kN-m outputs, signs, and tolerances derived outside the production code path.

- [severity: high] Acceptance criteria allow unresolved OCIMF/open physics questions through approval — The “Risks and Open Questions” section still includes “exact OCIMF generic vessel class/dataset row” and “exact simple area/drag rudder model coefficient/reference.” Those are not implementation details; they define the result. Recommended plan change: move both from open questions into approval-blocking decisions.

- [severity: medium] Cross-repo artifact governance is too loose — The plan names `digitalmodel` and `workspace-hub/acma-projects` outputs but does not require clean worktree checks, commit boundaries per repo, binary artifact handling policy, stale-output removal, or final push/issue-comment verification across both repos. Recommended plan change: add explicit preflight/closeout steps for both repos: `git status`, generated file manifest, legal scan where applicable, targeted tests, commits with pathspecs, push evidence, and issue comment links.

- [severity: medium] Output contract is ambiguous — “Markdown/HTML in digitalmodel” conflicts slightly with “durable revised Markdown report” and generated outputs under `digitalmodel/outputs/...`; Word/PDF names are not specified. Recommended plan change: list exact output filenames, which ones are source-controlled, which are generated-only, whether old `b1528_sirocco_moored_current_report.pdf` is overwritten or versioned, and what the manifest schema must contain.

- [severity: medium] “No resultant main presentation” test is not precise enough — The plan permits internal QA resultants but only tests broad labels in Markdown/HTML. This could accidentally leave resultants in tables, captions, chart metadata, or Word/PDF. Recommended plan change: define allowed vs banned occurrences of “resultant,” require checks across Markdown/HTML/Word/PDF-derived text where feasible, and explicitly allow resultants only in internal CSV/JSON QA if needed.

- [severity: medium] Plan-view schematic acceptance is hard to verify — The test names “transparent/simple ship outline, CoG marker, default values, X/Y/N arrows” but does not define what counts as passing for Markdown, HTML, Word, and PDF. Recommended plan change: require generated schematic source artifacts with stable IDs/alt text or metadata so tests can assert current/rudder section diagrams separately.

Blockers before `status:plan-review`:
- Resolve or gate the OCIMF coefficient source/provenance decision.
- Remove uncited invented force/moment formulas or replace them with a cited calculation contract.
- Define the simple rudder model basis before approval.
- Add numerical golden-case TDD oracles independent of production implementation.
- Tighten cross-repo output/commit/manifest acceptance criteria.

Answer to review question 1: not approval-ready. It needs revision before `status:plan-review`.
